  "ceiling": "AUDIT_ONLY structural/stoichiometric second-signal. It corroborates that the module's canonical EEW structure rule is self-consistent across the entire DGEBA oligomer series (not curve-fit to the n=0 monomer) and gives the mechanistic account of commercial-grade EEW elevation, but asserts nothing about the exact EEW of polydisperse commercial grades (measured composition required), product qualification, or cure conversion. Live runtime stays LOCKED_INTERNAL; the commercial_product_claim_locked=true lock is unchanged.",
  "claim": "An independent RDKit-2026.03.2 reference implementation extends the module's canonical EEW structure rule (EEW = M / n_epoxide) from the pure n=0 DGEBA monomer to the linear difunctional DGEBA oligomer SERIES. (1) The n=0 monomer reproduces the shipped Phase-0 expected EEW 170.2 g/eq (abs err 0.01, bar 0.5). (2) Four independently RDKit-constructed oligomers n=0..3 (C21H24O4, C39H44O7, C57H64O10, C75H84O13) each carry EXACTLY 2 terminal epoxide groups and are mass-additive: the bisphenol-A/2-hydroxy-propylene repeat mass is a byte-exact constant 284.355 g/mol across all three adjacent pairs (spread 0.0, max additivity deviation 0.0), so EEW(n) = 170.21 + 142.18*n exactly. (3) The mole-weighted number-average EEW_bar = 170.21 + 142.18*n_bar maps every published commercial DGEBA EEW band (liquid Epon 828/DER 331, near-monomer DER 332, semisolid Epon 1001F, solid Epon 1004F) to a non-negative n_bar that overlaps the independently published number-average degree of polymerization, mechanistically explaining why commercial grades read EEW > 170.2 WITHOUT asserting an exact EEW for the polydisperse mixture (composition is measured, not derived). (4) Four fail-closed controls (bisphenol-A 0 epoxide, phenyl glycidyl ether 1 epoxide, mono-hydrolyzed DGEBA 1 epoxide, fully advanced DGEBA-diol 0 epoxide) are all correctly excluded as non-difunctional-DGEBA exact anchors. IUPAC-2021 standard-atomic-weight uncertainty propagates to <=0.0085 g/eq on EEW(n=0), so the 0.5 g/eq acceptance bar carries ~59x headroom over fundamental atomic-mass uncertainty.",
